Third-party material in Repsilon

Figure meshes (app/src/main/resources/dev/gzclp/tracker/form/figure-*.bin and
hair.bin, baked from app/src/test/resources/dev/gzclp/tracker/form/body.bin
and shapes.bin)

  Made by tools/body-mesh.py from MakeHuman assets: the hm08 base mesh
  (makehuman/data/3dobjs/base.obj), the default skeleton
  (makehuman/data/rigs/default.mhskel), its skin weights
  (makehuman/data/rigs/default_weights.mhw), and the body and face morph
  targets that shape the six bodies (makehuman/data/targets/: macrodetails,
  torso, armslegs, hip, buttocks, measure, breast, neck, head, chin, nose,
  mouth, eyes, eyebrows, forehead and cheek), at commit
  a8bc2d54ff0ac92e78ff71431b1023eda42bf482 of
  https://github.com/makehumancommunity/makehuman

  Copyright (C) 2020-2021 Data Collection AB, Joel Palmius, Jonas Hauquier.
  Released under CC0 1.0 Universal (public domain dedication):
  https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

  The mesh is subdivided, its eye sockets and mouth closed over, decimated,
  posed and refitted to the app's skeleton. The hair is generated by the script
  on the mesh's scalp. MakeHuman's source code (AGPL)
  is not used or included.

